}

data cadence_tangent_demotion_note: String = "DEMOTED same day (reflection audit, captured 2026-08-02): an authored TangentReading is NOT an authority - its only mechanical check is that the referenced reason exists; it cannot establish fair prose, caused movement, counter motion, sufficiency, match-to-prior-focus, or that work is not an indefinite enabling chain. The rows below stay as retrospective SEED observations (marked, dated), and the replacement shape is planned-versus-observed reconciliation: (1) strategy revision in force at window start, (2) ex-ante declared focus, (3) observed state transition at window end - with the tangent regenerated as a narrative PROJECTION over those, never authored. Pilot: docs/strategy/2026-08-02-seven-day-evidence-packet.md. Dissolve-on: the generated projection replaces authored readings; TangentReading then becomes the projection's output type or is deleted."

data cadence_tangent_note: String = "Layered reflection (operator request 2026-08-02): read the ONE venture timeline at five smoothing windows - the tangent at scale tau. A TangentReading is a dated OBSERVATION of the direction of movement inside one window, with receipts for what actually moved (magnitude_evidence) and a projects_onto edge into the same StrategicReason authority the lane bindings use - so alignment is not prose, it is a resolvable join: a reading whose reason does not resolve is orphan movement (moving where no declared goal points), witnessed exactly like lane bindings. The dual failure the layers must catch: (1) ORPHAN MOVEMENT - a short-window tangent projecting onto nothing declared; (2) STARVED AXIS - a declared long-horizon objective whose short-window tangents are zero across many windows (the 0/27 producer counter sitting still for months is the live specimen; the audit's reforecast triggers are starved-axis alarms). Direction alignment is NOT magnitude sufficiency - a window can point exactly at the goal and move nothing - so the refinement path is CounterObservation rows (dated counter values with evidence; tangents DERIVED by differencing, never stored) once the weekly counter vocabulary stabilizes on the audit's section-8 set. Readings accumulate; per-(window,date) unique."

type CadenceWindow
  = DailyWindow
  | WeeklyWindow
  | MonthlyWindow
  | QuarterlyWindow
  | YearlyWindow

type TangentReading {
  window: CadenceWindow
  read_on: String
  direction: String
  magnitude_evidence: EvidenceAnchor
  projects_onto: StrategicReason
}

data acquisition_grounding_note: String = "The acquisition funnel mechanism was dissolved into its public authority on 2026-08-01 after PR 7557 merged: gunbc.econ.acquisition owns the generic N-stage scenario, exact-fraction ConversionRate (std.algebra FieldOfFractions at Nat), MoneyOnce entry cost, typed per-stage refusals, and the AcquisitionCostForecast carrier whose structural forecast-vs-observation distinctness the kernel controls now cite. The private duplicates (Forecast, Observation, ConversionRate, AcquisitionScenario, ScenarioInput, ForecastRefusalCause, CacForecastResult, forecast_cost_per_activated) were deleted in favor of importing the authority; the private graph keeps only its INSTANTIATIONS (declared scenarios with their provenance) in strategy.gunbc_strategy."

data program_contract_note: String = "Program decomposition and discharge graph (operator-endorsed audit 2026-08-02, docs/strategy/2026-08-02-program-decomposition-audit.md). The relation the reflection thread was missing: which exact obligation of which exact contract does a piece of work discharge, and why do the children jointly suffice for the parent. StrategicContract is a durable authority whose criteria are amendable only through a ContractAmendment carrying the operator DecisionReceipt - the ruling AUTHORIZES the amendment, the amended contract is the authority, the verbatim conversation stays opaque provenance in docs/strategy (this supersedes the StrategyRevision-carrier-as-spine proposal). StrategicObligation rows project what remains to be proven; ProgramDecomposition states whether the children are jointly sufficient (CompleteCoverage requires its own DecisionReceipt, PartialCoverage names what is unproven); WorkContribution binds ONE work ref to ONE exact obligation with the maximum conclusion it may claim. Invalidation is by construction, not grep: strategy_criteria_digest derives the digest from criteria content (the digest IS the joined criteria text, never a field authored beside it), every binding and decomposition carries the digest LITERAL it was read against, so amending the contract mechanically mismatches every un-reread downstream row (ContributionStale). External state enters only as dated ObservationReceipt rows with a typed ObservedOutcome and a subject revision; no present-tense copy is stored, and a landed PR is not roadmap acceptance - discharge derivation requires ObservedLanded on a fresh discharging binding, and contract completion additionally requires the decomposition itself Complete. Deferred with the audit: FocusSelection and scheduling edge kinds (selection is not refinement; a week without an ex-ante focus renders as cadence-comparison-unavailable, never a repo-wide red), and retroactive backfill under three distinct historical claim kinds (DecisionMadeAtTheTime, RetrospectivelyAttributedContribution, CurrentInterpretationOfPastPeriod)."

type StrategicContract {
  id: String
  statement: String
  acceptance_criteria: List<String>
  constraint_ids: List<String>
  adoption: DecisionReceipt
}

type ObligationAcceptanceKind
  = ByExecutionReceipt
  | ByObservationReceipt
  | ByOperatorJudgment

type StrategicObligation {
  id: String
  parent_contract: String
  subject: String
  required_conclusion: String
  acceptance_kind: ObligationAcceptanceKind
}

type DecompositionCoverage
  = PartialCoverage { open_note: String }
  | CompleteCoverage { receipt: DecisionReceipt }

type ProgramDecomposition {
  id: String
  parent_contract: String
  parent_criteria_digest: String
  child_obligation_ids: List<String>
  composition_rule: String
  coverage: DecompositionCoverage
}

type ContributionKind
  = DischargesObligation
  | PreservesAcceptedState
  | BoundedExploration { bound: String }
  | MeasurementForDecision { decision_question_id: String }
  | ClosesPrerequisite

type WorkContribution {
  id: String
  work_ref: String
  obligation_id: String
  kind: ContributionKind
  maximum_conclusion: String
  parent_criteria_digest: String
}

type ContractAmendment {
  id: String
  subject_contract: String
  previous_criteria: List<String>
  summary: String
  receipt: DecisionReceipt
  evidence: String
}

type ObservedOutcome
  = ObservedLanded
  | ObservedInFlight
  | ObservedWithdrawn

type ObservationReceipt {
  id: String
  subject: String
  observed_on: String
  subject_revision: String
  outcome: ObservedOutcome
  result: String
  evidence: EvidenceAnchor
}

fn strategy_criteria_digest(criteria: List<String>) -> String {
  fold(criteria, init: "criteria", f: fn(acc, c) { "{acc}|{c}" })
}

fn strategy_contract_digest(c: StrategicContract) -> String {
  strategy_criteria_digest(criteria: c.acceptance_criteria)
}

type ContributionStatus
  = ContributionStale { bound_digest: String, current_digest: String }
  | ContributionUnobserved
  | ContributionObserved { outcome: ObservedOutcome, observed_on: String }

fn strategy_contribution_status(b: WorkContribution, contract: StrategicContract, observations: List<ObservationReceipt>) -> ContributionStatus {
  let current = strategy_contract_digest(c: contract)
  if !(b.parent_criteria_digest == current) {
    ContributionStale { bound_digest: b.parent_criteria_digest, current_digest: current }
  } else {
    fold(observations, init: ContributionUnobserved, f: fn(acc, o) {
      if o.subject == b.work_ref { ContributionObserved { outcome: o.outcome, observed_on: o.observed_on } } else { acc }
    })
  }
}

fn strategy_binding_is_discharging(b: WorkContribution) -> Bool {
  match b.kind {
    DischargesObligation => true
    PreservesAcceptedState => false
    BoundedExploration { bound } => false
    MeasurementForDecision { decision_question_id } => false
    ClosesPrerequisite => false
  }
}

fn strategy_obligation_bound_fresh(obligation_id: String, current_digest: String, bindings: List<WorkContribution>) -> Bool {
  fold(bindings, init: false, f: fn(acc, b) {
    acc || (b.obligation_id == obligation_id && strategy_binding_is_discharging(b: b) && b.parent_criteria_digest == current_digest)
  })
}

fn strategy_observed_landed(work_ref: String, observations: List<ObservationReceipt>) -> Bool {
  fold(observations, init: false, f: fn(acc, o) {
    acc || (o.subject == work_ref && match o.outcome { ObservedLanded => true  ObservedInFlight => false  ObservedWithdrawn => false })
  })
}

fn strategy_obligation_discharge_observed(obligation_id: String, current_digest: String, bindings: List<WorkContribution>, observations: List<ObservationReceipt>) -> Bool {
  fold(bindings, init: false, f: fn(acc, b) {
    acc
      || (b.obligation_id == obligation_id
            && strategy_binding_is_discharging(b: b)
            && b.parent_criteria_digest == current_digest
            && strategy_observed_landed(work_ref: b.work_ref, observations: observations))
  })
}

type ObligationSearch
  = NoObligationFound
  | FoundObligation { obligation_id: String }

fn strategy_first_unbound_child(contract_id: String, current_digest: String, decompositions: List<ProgramDecomposition>, bindings: List<WorkContribution>) -> ObligationSearch {
  fold(decompositions, init: NoObligationFound, f: fn(acc, d) {
    if d.parent_contract == contract_id {
      fold(d.child_obligation_ids, init: acc, f: fn(a2, oid) {
        match a2 {
          FoundObligation { obligation_id } => a2
          NoObligationFound =>
            if strategy_obligation_bound_fresh(obligation_id: oid, current_digest: current_digest, bindings: bindings) {
              NoObligationFound
            } else {
              FoundObligation { obligation_id: oid }
            }
        }
      })
    } else {
      acc
    }
  })
}

fn strategy_first_undischarged_child(contract_id: String, current_digest: String, decompositions: List<ProgramDecomposition>, bindings: List<WorkContribution>, observations: List<ObservationReceipt>) -> ObligationSearch {
  fold(decompositions, init: NoObligationFound, f: fn(acc, d) {
    if d.parent_contract == contract_id {
      fold(d.child_obligation_ids, init: acc, f: fn(a2, oid) {
        match a2 {
          FoundObligation { obligation_id } => a2
          NoObligationFound =>
            if strategy_obligation_discharge_observed(obligation_id: oid, current_digest: current_digest, bindings: bindings, observations: observations) {
              NoObligationFound
            } else {
              FoundObligation { obligation_id: oid }
            }
        }
      })
    } else {
      acc
    }
  })
}

type ContractCompletionRefusalCause
  = DecompositionMissing
  | DecompositionNotSingular
  | DecompositionStale
  | DecompositionPartial
  | ObligationUnbound { obligation_id: String }
  | ObligationUndischarged { obligation_id: String }

type ContractCompletion
  = ContractComplete
  | ContractCompletionRefused { cause: ContractCompletionRefusalCause }

fn strategy_contract_completion(contract: StrategicContract, decompositions: List<ProgramDecomposition>, bindings: List<WorkContribution>, observations: List<ObservationReceipt>) -> ContractCompletion {
  let current = strategy_contract_digest(c: contract)
  let dec_count = fold(decompositions, init: 0, f: fn(acc, d) { if d.parent_contract == contract.id { acc + 1 } else { acc } })
  if dec_count == 0 {
    ContractCompletionRefused { cause: DecompositionMissing }
  } else {
    if !(dec_count == 1) {
      ContractCompletionRefused { cause: DecompositionNotSingular }
    } else {
      let stale = fold(decompositions, init: false, f: fn(acc, d) {
        acc || (d.parent_contract == contract.id && !(d.parent_criteria_digest == current))
      })
      if stale {
        ContractCompletionRefused { cause: DecompositionStale }
      } else {
        let partial = fold(decompositions, init: false, f: fn(acc, d) {
          acc || (d.parent_contract == contract.id && match d.coverage { PartialCoverage { open_note } => true  CompleteCoverage { receipt } => false })
        })
        if partial {
          ContractCompletionRefused { cause: DecompositionPartial }
        } else {
          match strategy_first_unbound_child(contract_id: contract.id, current_digest: current, decompositions: decompositions, bindings: bindings) {
            FoundObligation { obligation_id } => ContractCompletionRefused { cause: ObligationUnbound { obligation_id: obligation_id } }
            NoObligationFound =>
              match strategy_first_undischarged_child(contract_id: contract.id, current_digest: current, decompositions: decompositions, bindings: bindings, observations: observations) {
                FoundObligation { obligation_id } => ContractCompletionRefused { cause: ObligationUndischarged { obligation_id: obligation_id } }
                NoObligationFound => ContractComplete
              }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

data contribution_kind_discipline_note: String = "Recut per the discharge-graph review (operator-routed 2026-08-02, docs/strategy/2026-08-02-discharge-graph-review.md). Three rules. (1) A work prerequisite is modeled as its own narrower OBLIGATION plus an ObligationPrerequisite edge, and the parent-unblocking effect is DERIVED (strategy_blockers_discharged) - never authored as a contribution kind; ClosesPrerequisite is retained only for prerequisites that are not work obligations (an operator decision, an external release, a dated observation, an approval), and it has zero uses in the facts today. (2) A ContributionKind belongs to one contribution EDGE, never to a PR globally - one PR may carry several independently evidenced rows. (3) CompleteCoverage is not an operator verdict: the operator authorizes the contract boundary and the coverage RULE; completeness must then be DERIVED from a declared population (first instance: the self-host module denominator derived from the public compiler_frontier_roster). The four-step measurement ladder is derivable, never conflated: machinery exists != measurement happened != measurement supports a choice != choice was made; MeasurementReadiness carries the middle distinction, and a selection derives from the declared rule when the measurement exists, escalating to the operator only on genuine incomparability."

type ObligationPrerequisite {
  blocker_obligation: String
  blocked_obligation: String
}

fn strategy_blocker_count(obligation_id: String, prerequisites: List<ObligationPrerequisite>) -> Nat {
  fold(prerequisites, init: 0, f: fn(acc, p) { if p.blocked_obligation == obligation_id { acc + 1 } else { acc } })
}

fn strategy_blockers_discharged(obligation_id: String, current_digest: String, prerequisites: List<ObligationPrerequisite>, bindings: List<WorkContribution>, observations: List<ObservationReceipt>) -> Bool {
  fold(prerequisites, init: true, f: fn(acc, p) {
    acc
      && (!(p.blocked_obligation == obligation_id)
            || strategy_obligation_discharge_observed(obligation_id: p.blocker_obligation, current_digest: current_digest, bindings: bindings, observations: observations))
  })
}

type MeasurementReadiness
  = MeasurementAbsent { missing: String }
  | MeasurementPresent { observation_id: String }

fn strategy_measurement_readiness(subject: String, observations: List<ObservationReceipt>) -> MeasurementReadiness {
  fold(observations, init: MeasurementAbsent { missing: subject }, f: fn(acc, o) {
    if o.subject == subject { MeasurementPresent { observation_id: o.id } } else { acc }
  })
}

fn strategy_program_view(contract: StrategicContract, obligations: List<StrategicObligation>, bindings: List<WorkContribution>) -> List<String> {
  let current = strategy_contract_digest(c: contract)
  fold(obligations, init: [], f: fn(acc, o) {
    if o.parent_contract == contract.id {
      let oid = o.id
      if strategy_obligation_bound_fresh(obligation_id: oid, current_digest: current, bindings: bindings) {
        concat(acc, ["{oid} BOUND"])
      } else {
        concat(acc, ["{oid} OPEN"])
      }
    } else {
      acc
    }
  })
}
